[candidate · 6:53] Beans were only a quarter of COGS, so the story is the other 75%. Old COGS was 42 points of revenue; the non-bean portion was 31.5 of those. Up 37.5%, that adds ~11.8 points on its own — call it three-quarters of the 16-point increase, before any bean move. So dairy, packaging and food are the driver, not coffee.

That flips the sourcing plan: hedging beans is the wrong lever. Focus on dairy contracts and portion control, packaging spec and supplier consolidation, and food — which is probably the lowest-margin category and may be dragging mix. Price increases should be weighted to food and milk-alternative add-ons specifically.
