[candidate · 8:21] Fair — I was sloppy. 42 and 31.5 are index points of old revenue, base 100. Non-bean up 37.5% gives 43.3, so +11.8 index points.

But today's revenue is 115, and COGS is 58% of that = 66.7 index points. Old COGS was 42, so total COGS grew 24.7 index points. The non-bean 11.8 is under half of that, not three-quarters — my error. As a share of today's revenue, 11.8/115 ≈ 10.3 points, versus the 16-point margin swing.

The rest has to be beans rising too, and the fact that 15% more volume carries more input cost regardless of price per unit. So it's broad input inflation across the basket, amplified by volume, with zero price pass-through.
